# Per-package BASH environment for app-office/libreoffice — portage sources
# /etc/portage/env/${CATEGORY}/${PN} as bash in the ebuild environment (unlike
# the package.env-referenced *.conf files, which are key=value only).
#
# WHY: LibreOffice refuses to compile as root. Its top-level Makefile.in ships
#
#     check-if-root:
#         @if test ! `uname` = 'Haiku' -a `id -u` = 0 && test -z $$container; then \
#             if test ! -x "$$(command -v systemd-detect-virt)" || ! systemd-detect-virt -c -q; then \
#                 echo 'Building LibreOffice as root is a very bad idea, use a regular user.'; \
#                 exit 1; \
#             fi \
#         fi
#
# and EVERY package in this stage4 builds as root: specs-x86/portage/make.conf.tmpl
# sets FEATURES="... -userpriv -usersandbox ..." (deliberately — the chroot has no
# usable portage-user ownership over the bind-mounted scratch), so `id -u` is 0 and
# there is no systemd-detect-virt in the seed. Result, reproduced on two consecutive
# standalone-unaffiliated prod builds (out/sessions/20260725-061608-978c99 and
# 20260725-140638-09692d):
#
#     Building LibreOffice as root is a very bad idea, use a regular user.
#     make: *** [Makefile:72: check-if-root] Error 1
#     >>> Failed to emerge app-office/libreoffice-25.2.7.2-r1
#
# Because the payload emerge runs --keep-going, that did NOT abort the build — the
# 061608 session went on to emit a full set of "prod" artifacts (.img.xz/.iso/
# .stage4.tar.xz) with NO office suite on an image whose whole point is a capable
# desktop. (The companion fix for that silent degradation is the requested-atom
# completeness gate in build-x86-host-stage4.sh.)
#
# THE FIX: upstream's own escape hatch. `test -z $container` is the FIRST branch of
# that guard: a non-empty `container` makes the whole check a no-op, which is
# precisely how distro/CI builds inside containers pass it (the same variable
# systemd sets to advertise a container payload). Our chroot IS that case, so the
# value is honest rather than a workaround: we are building inside a chroot.
#
# NOT FORCE_BUILD_AS_ROOT: that variable does not exist in LibreOffice 25.2's
# Makefile.in (verified against the real distfile, not from memory). NOT
# per-package FEATURES=userpriv either: the portage user cannot own the
# bind-mounted build scratch in this chroot, which is why userpriv is off
# fleet-wide in the first place.
#
# Scoped to this one package on purpose: `container` is read by other software
# (systemd-detect-virt consumers, some ebuilds' container-aware branches), so it
# must NOT go in make.conf where it would reach every package in the image.
export container="chroot"
